Resolves: #210

# Why

When using a font family with multiple files for each font weight, the CSS rules generated for the web export is incorrect and does not properly define the font family.

# How

Currently, `useFonts` is called as:

```ts
useFonts({
  "WixMadeforText": {
    uri: require("@/assets/fonts/WixMadeforText-Regular.woff2"),
    display: FontDisplay.AUTO,
  }
})
```

With this PR, we can call the `useFonts` function with a richer configuration for italics and multiple font weights.

```ts
useFonts({
  "WixMadeforText-Regular": {
    uri: require("@/assets/fonts/WixMadeforText-Regular.woff2"),
    family: "Wix Madefor Text",
    style: "normal",
    weight: 400,
    display: FontDisplay.AUTO,
  },
  "WixMadeforText-Italic": {
    uri: require("@/assets/fonts/WixMadeforText-Italic.woff2")
    family: "Wix Madefor Text",
    style: "italic",
    weight: 400,
    display: FontDisplay.AUTO,
  },
  // ...
})
```

When generating the CSS, each named font produces the correct CSS.

```css
@font-face {
	font-family: ...;
	src: ...;
	font-display: ...;
	font-weight: ...;
	font-style: ...;
}
```

Each font can then be properly used on the web by specifying the font family, weight, and style independently.

# Test Plan

I've added this patch to my private multi-platform project and fonts are correctly loaded on the web now.
